      "content": "Here's a revised paragraph that takes a stronger stance on the limitations of traditional conservation methods:\n\nThe traditional conservation model, which often prioritizes human interests over ecological integrity, relies on outdated notions of control and manipulation to stabilize ecosystems. However, a multitude of studies reveal that the very practices intended to conserve biodiversity – such as prescribed burns, fencing, and habitat fragmentation – ultimately undermine long-term ecological resilience and promote cumulative extirpation of species. These \"managed\" conservation methods are, in reality, an attempt to impose a fragile human imprint on the natural world, rather than embracing the ephemeral and unpredictable nature of ecosystems.",
